==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈæswaɪp/|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
{{compound|ass|wipe|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|vulgar|lang=en}} An [[annoying]], [[contemptible]], or [[worthless]] person.
#: ''He is such an '''asswipe'''!''
# {{context|British|informal|vulgar|lang=en}} [[toilet paper|Toilet paper]].
#* '''1976''', Micheal Clodfelter, ''The Pawns of Dishonor'',<sup >[http://books.google.com/books?id=hffbAAAAIAAJ ]</sup> Branden Press, ISBN 9780828315876, page 249:
#*: I rapidly expended my own and everyone else’s supply of tiny [[w:Meal, Combat, Individual ration|C-ration]] rolls of '''asswipe''' and was reduced to wiping my nasty behind with leaves and grass.
#* '''1983''', Nicholas Proffitt, ''Gardens of Stone'',<sup >[http://books.google.com/books?id=2FWxAAAAIAAJ ]</sup> Carroll & Graf, ISBN 9780881840179, page 317:
#*: “{{...}} Into your packs you put your toilet articles, mess kits, extra socks, and skivvies and longjohns if you have them. If you have a roll of '''asswipe''', put that in, too. {{...}}”<!-- [sic] quotation marks in original -->
#* '''2008''', Joseph Heywood, ''Death Roe: A Woods Cop Mystery'',<sup >[http://books.google.com/books?id=AQe3ujxs4VQC ][http://www.amazon.com/Death-Roe-Woods-Mystery-Mysteries/dp/1599214288 ]</sup> Globe Pequot, ISBN 9781599214283, page 252:
#*: “I doubt a dime would buy a single square of '''asswipe''' in this city, {{...}}” <!-- [sic] quotation marks in original -->
# {{context|figuratively|lang=en}} A [[periodical]] which has the habit of publishing questionable truths.
#: ''Our local paper is an '''asswipe'''''.

